{"id":"claim:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu--the-sakhalin-ainu-word-tuuki-sake-cup-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu","topics":["topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu","topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu--phonological-adaptation"],"statement":{"en":"The Sakhalin Ainu word tuuki 'sake cup' is a loanword from Japanese (Old Japanese tuki HL) whose long vowel /uu/ developed secondarily from an accented open initial syllable.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語の tuuki「杯」は日本語（上代日本語 tuki HL）からの借用語であり、その長母音 /uu/ はアクセントのある第1開音節から二次的に生じたものである。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"example_only","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["tuuki","túki"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0018-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu--japanese-tu-tsu-is-frequently-adapted-as-ci","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu","topics":["topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu","topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu--phonological-adaptation"],"statement":{"en":"Japanese /tu/ (tsu) is frequently adapted as ci in loanwords, e.g. CIITE for Japanese tsuite.","ja":"日本語の「つ」はアイヌ語借用語で ci として発音されることが多い（例：CIITE「搗いて」）。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":["in loanwords from Japanese"]},"forms":["ci","CIITE"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0043-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu--since-ainu-lacks-palatalized-glide-onsets-like-kya","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu","topics":["topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu","topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu--phonological-adaptation"],"statement":{"en":"Since Ainu lacks palatalized glide onsets like kya, kyu, and kyo, Japanese contracted sounds (yōon) are often expanded into two syllables such as kiya or kiyu (e.g. TOOKIYO 'Tokyo'), though cha, chu, and cho are sometimes rendered as ca, cu, and co (e.g. KAPOCA 'squash/pumpkin').","ja":"アイヌ語には「きゃ」「きゅ」「きょ」のような拗音が無いため、日本語の拗音は kiya、kiyu のように2音節に展開されることが多いが（例：TOOKIYO「東京」）、「ちゃ」「ちゅ」「ちょ」は ca、cu、co で写されることがある（例：KAPOCA「かぼちゃ」）。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":["in loanwords from Japanese"]},"forms":["kiya","kiyu","ca","cu","co","TOOKIYO","KAPOCA"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0043-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu--in-hokkaido-ainu-the-japanese-loan-sato-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu","topics":["topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu","topic:contact/japanese-loanwords-in-ainu--semantic-distribution"],"statement":{"en":"In Hokkaido Ainu, the Japanese loan sato is used for 'sugar', whereas in Sakhalin dialects only otoopenpe 'something sweet' is found.","ja":"北海道アイヌ語では「砂糖」を表すのに日本語からの借用語satoが用いられるが、樺太方言ではより広い「甘いもの」を意味するotoopenpeのみが見られる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["sato","otoopenpe"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shiraishitangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0046-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
